-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
PART C — what this changes, and one decision left open
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
Compression would explain every observation in one mechanism: too-small sigma on
high-volatility names produces the |z|>3 exceedances; those few items dominate
the RMS and so the 0.733 calibration ratio; the rank-based PIT barely moves,
which is why it looks uniform; and the body's MAD-scale sits near 1.0 because
the middle of the cross-section is fine.

If so, NONE of ADR 0032's family is the right correction. A location shift, a
scale factor and a Student-t all act uniformly across items; a cross-sectional
mis-allocation needs a per-item map -- expanding log sigma toward the baseline's
spread. That is a different Phase 3 than the one pre-registered.

OPEN AND NOT DECIDED HERE: the ambiguous-band pre-registration (records 2 and 4)
does NOT include the compression statistics, because it was written before this
analysis existed. Adding them is a governance decision, not mine to take
silently, and there is still time -- the band is at 23 of 353 and has scored
nothing. PROPOSED, for approval or rejection before it finishes:

    on the ambiguous band, the same two selection-free statements --
      (i)  slope and CI of log sigma_MAP on log sigma_RW, plus the spread ratio
      (ii) median sigma_MAP/sigma_RW on the top 11/18/36 by |realised return|
           versus the rest, with cluster-robust CIs
    prediction: slope well below 1, spread ratio near 0.5, all three cuts
    negative and excluding zero
    if it does not replicate, volatility compression is withdrawn and ADR 0032's
